UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '此处详列了我们在洛克莫丹藏匿情报、等待接应期间所使用的全部地点。若你设法从探险者协会或其盟友手中取得任何文件，请将其放置在这些地点之一，我们的一名信使将在一周之内取走包裹，并送至我们的行动基地。$B$B在你记熟本书中的所有地点之后，请将其烧毁，以免落入敌手。若你因任何理由怀疑敌人已对你的行动产生怀疑，请立即烧掉本书。无论如何，此书都绝不能落入敌手，否则我们的联络路线将被破坏。$B$B为了拉格纳罗斯！' WHERE `ID` = 3550 AND `Text` = 'Detailed here in are all of the locations used to secret our information within Loch Modan while awaiting pickup. Should you manage to obtain any documents from the Explorer\'s League or their allies， place them in one of these locations and one of our messengers will pick the package up within the week for delivery to our base of operations.$B$BOnce you have memorized all of the locations within this book， burn it so that it cannot be obtained by our enemies. Should you suspect for any reason that our enemies might be suspicious of your activities， burn the book immediately. By no means should this ever fall into enemy hands， lest our routes of communication be compromised.$B$BFor Ragnaros！';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '地点一：西部洛克湖码头\n\n石锤镇东北方有一处小屋和一座码头，钓鱼季节偶有矮人使用。请将包裹装入防水容器，藏在码头下方不易被察觉之处。$B$B该地点的投递与取件只应在夜间进行，以降低被附近渔民目击的风险。由于显而易见的原因，钓鱼季节期间该投递点的优先级将降低。' WHERE `ID` = 3551 AND `Text` = 'Location 1：Western Loch Dock\n\r\n\rNortheast of Thelsamar， there is a small dwelling and a dock that are utilized by dwarves on occasion during fishing season. Store the package in a watertight container under the dock， out of sight.$B$BDrop offs and pickups from this location should occur only at night as to reduce risk of being witnessed by fishermen in the area. This dropoff point will recieve reduced priority during the fishing season for obvious reasons.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '地点二：灰爪巢穴\n\n石锤镇以南有一座大山。山的南侧有一条小径通往山顶的洞穴。请将包裹存放在洞穴深处的岩石后面。$B$B请勿继续将该洞穴用作避难所或藏身处。将其用于此类用途会危及我们的包裹与信使路线的安全。' WHERE `ID` = 3552 AND `Text` = 'Location 2：Grizzlepaw Den\n\r\n\rSouth of Thelsamar， there is a large hill. On the south side of the hill， there is a path leading to the cave at the top. Store packges behind the rocks in the back of the cave.$B$BPlease refrain from continued use of this cave as a shelter and/or hideout. Utilizing this cave for such compromises the security of our packages and our messenger routes.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '地点三：珊达的巢穴\n\n挖掘场西南方有一间小屋，曾属于一位离群索居的隐士。$B然而珊达在这处洞穴里安了家，把所有可能入住者都赶走了。洞口正外侧是绝佳的投递点。$B$B提醒一句：珊达是一只体型堪比两个矮人的巨大杀人蜘蛛。切勿把文件投入洞内——即便珊达眼下不在，只要给它时间，它总会回来的。' WHERE `ID` = 3553 AND `Text` = 'Location 3：Shanda\'s Lair\n\r\n\rThere is a small hovel to the southwest of the excavation site that once belonged to a reclusive hermit.$BShanda\'s residence in this cave， however， has driven all potential inhabitants away. Just outside the mouth of the cave serves as a perfect drop point.$B$BAs a reminder， Shanda is an enormous murderous spider the size of two dwarves. Do not drop documents IN the cave， even if Shanda is not currently present she will be， given time.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '地点四：铁带的小室\n\n铁带挖掘场正中央有一条侧道通向一处隐蔽且已废弃的壁龛。它就藏在探险者协会的眼皮底下，是极佳的投递点。$B$B穴居人已经牵制了探险者协会的注意力，但别忘了他们对我们同样怀有敌意。夜间前往该处时要小心，穴居人可能正埋伏着。' WHERE `ID` = 3554 AND `Text` = 'Location 4：Ironband\'s Cubby\n\r\n\rA side passage in the heart of Ironband\'s Excavation Site leads up to a well——hidden and disused alcove. Hidden right under the noses of the Explorer\'s league， this is a prime dropoff spot.$B$BThe Troggs have distracted the Explorer\'s League， but do not forget they are still hostile to us. Take care when accessing the site at night， Troggs may be waiting in ambush.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '地点五：莫格拉什骷髅神像\n\n这座石制骷髅神像看上去像是食人魔地盘的一部分，但实际位置比食人魔活动的范围更靠南。请把文件放在它的底座处。$B$B绝不要把文件放进骷髅神像的嘴里。已有数份文件因此永久丢失，还有一只手也神秘地不见了。' WHERE `ID` = 3555 AND `Text` = 'Location 5：Mo\'grash Skull Idol\n\r\n\rThis stone skull idol seems like part of the ogre grounds， but is further south than the ogres actually roam. Place documents at the base of it.$B$BDo NOT place documents IN the mouth of the skull idol. Several documents have been permanently lost this way， as well as one hand， mysteriously.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '地点六：洛克湖中的小树林\n\n洛克湖中央一小片长着三株树苗的树林，是一处十分偏僻的投递点。$B$B湖水退去后，这一带已不再那么偏僻，好在鳄鱼帮了不少忙。' WHERE `ID` = 3556 AND `Text` = 'Location 6：The Grove in the Loch\n\r\n\rA small grove of three saplings in the center of the Loch serves as a well——isolated drop off point.$B$BDraining of the Loch has left this space slightly less isolated. The crocolisks have helped to mitigate this.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '杜拉克，$B$B这位$R协助我收集了足够的邪火，用来向精灵发起攻击。$B$B这些弹药将极具毁灭性——但根本无法控制。我需要一种方法来引导它们的弹道。$B$B只要碎木岗哨得以保全，我干扰恶魔力量的事想必终会得到宽恕……$B$B德拉卡' WHERE `ID` = 3559 AND `Text` = 'Durak，$B$BThis $R has assisted me IN collecting enough fel fire TO launch an assault ON the elves.$B$BThe projectiles will be devastating——but impossible TO control. I need a way TO direct their trajectory.$B$BI\'m sure to be forgiven for meddling with demonic powers once Splintertree is saved……$B$BDraaka';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '<药剂师的笔记字迹又小又挤，其间夹杂着复杂的炼金公式，以及孩童涂鸦般的骷髅与闪电。眯起眼睛，你能辨认出最近一段的一部分：>$B$B……最壮丽的腐化，深深嵌入活体组织之中。经由食物链<几个字被抹花>后极具传染性。今日的试验确认，它的起源只有部分是生物性的。邪蹄，我那位<难以辨认>的同伴，一心想着复仇，对自身更为“建设性”的用途视而不见<一段绿色脓液染污了本段其余部分>。研究进展缓慢。但愿我在奥尔塔拉克斯的同伴们运气好些。' WHERE `ID` = 3561 AND `Text` = '<The Apothecary\'s notes are scribbled in a cramped hand， with complex alchemic formulas interspersed among childlike doodles of skulls and lightning bolts. Squinting， you can make out parts of a recent passage：>$B$B……most magnificent corruption， embedding itself deep within living tissue. Extremely contagious when <several words are smudged> via food chain. Today\'s tests confirm it is only partially biological in origin. Foulhoof， my <illegible> companion， preoccupied with vengeance and blind to the more \'constructive\' applications of his <a greenish ichor stains the remainder of the paragraph.> Research progresses slowly. Hope my companions at Althalaxx fare better.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '裂牙，$B$B我从碎木岗哨向你汇报，消息并不乐观。$B$B前哨最近遭到卡多雷袭击，导致任何报告都无法送出。$B$B围困已被打破，但我们损失了许多人，而且下一次进攻似乎迫在眉睫。$B$B只要命运允许，我们就会继续把精灵送进坟墓。$B$B——卡德拉克' WHERE `ID` = 3566 AND `Text` = 'Grimfang，$B$BI report to you from Splintertree， and the news is unpleasant.$B$BThe post was recently attacked by the kaldorei， which prevented any reports from being delivered.$B$BThe siege has been broken， but many were lost and another attack looks imminent.$B$BWe shall continue sending elves to their graves as long as fate permits.$B$B——Kadrak';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '<br /><br />纪念</h1><br />沙尔丁、格沙拉、沃尔科</h1>以及那些再也没能回家的人。</h1>' WHERE `ID` = 3567 AND `Text` = '<br /><br />In Memory</h1><br />Shaldyn， Gershala， Volcor</h1>and those who never made it home.</h1>';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '<这块小小的墓碑上温柔地刻着兽人符文。><br /><br />$B$B$B$B$B——挚爱的奥尔格拉——<br />$B$B$B$B$B$B$B$B曼克里克之妻<br /><br />$B$B$B我花了很久才找到你<br />$B$B$B$B$B如今你却已不在' WHERE `ID` = 3568 AND `Text` = '<The small grave marker is lovingly inscribed with orcish runes.><br /><br />$B$B$B$B$B——BELOVED OLGRA——<br />$B$B$B$B$B$B$B$BWife of Mankrik<br /><br />$B$B$BIt took forever to find you<br />$B$B$B$B$BAnd now you are gone';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '第一天：\n\n上了一艘名叫“德拉卡的怒火”的船。$B我们要把特殊货物运到海对岸的远方。$B我在船上负责打扫，上岸后负责侦察。\n\n这活儿总比在奥格瑞玛搜捕联盟盗贼和德鲁伊强。\n\n食物不如从前，但格罗格酒味道一样。$B杜隆塔尔已经消失在视野之外。' WHERE `ID` = 3570 AND `Text` = 'Day One：\r\n\r\nGot on a ship called Draka\'s Fury.$BWe\'re taking the special cargo to a far away place across the ocean.$BI have the duty to clean stuff on the ship and scout when we get to land.\r\n\r\nBetter work than searching for Alliance rogues and druids in Orgrimmar.\r\n\r\nThe food is not as good， but the grog tastes the same.$BDurotar has already slipped out of sight.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '第二天：\n\n食物和船的摇晃让我吃不消！\n\n要打扫的地方很多，因为我的许多兄弟都晕船了。$B我总觉得这不是什么好主意，但既然他要去，我们也乐意跟着他沉到海底。\n\n希望不至于走到那一步。' WHERE `ID` = 3571 AND `Text` = 'Day Two：\r\n\r\nThe food and rocking of the ship do not agree with me！\r\n\r\nThere is much to clean as there are many of my brothers who are sick.$BThis does not seem like a good idea to me， but if he needs to go， we will gladly follow him to the bottom of the sea.\r\n\r\nLet us hope that it does not come to that.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '第三天：\n\n海浪猛烈拍打着船身。$B船长让我们收起船帆。$B我们就像巨浪中的孩童玩具。\n\n我或许不喜欢大海，但今天我像个真正的战士一样把食物留在了肚子里。' WHERE `ID` = 3572 AND `Text` = 'Day Three：\r\n\r\nThe sea lashes the ship very heavily.$BThe captain had us take down the sails.$BWe are like a child\'s toy in the middle of gigantic waves.\r\n\r\nI may not like the ocean， but I kept my food down today like a true warrior.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '第四天：\n\n地平线上出现了两座小岛。$B船长说我们只会从它们旁边驶过。$B他不想停靠。$B他语气里有种我不喜欢的紧绷感。$B那听起来像是恐惧。\n\n有很多事要做……什么？$B外面传来爆炸声。$B我上甲板去看看怎么回事。' WHERE `ID` = 3573 AND `Text` = 'Day Four：\r\n\r\nThere are two small islands on the horizon.$BThe captain says that we will sail just past them.$BHe does not want to stop.$BThere is an edge to his voice that I do not like.$BIt sounds like fear.\r\n\r\nThere was much to do…… what？$BThere are sounds of explosions outside.$BI am going above deck to see what it is.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '第？？天：\n\n我被冲上了一座岛的岩石海岸。$B一定是我先前看到的那两座岛之一。$B我的兄弟大多已经死了。$B我们的特殊货物不见踪影。$B我害怕最坏的结果，不敢相信自己的念头。\n\n我不知道过去了多少天。$B一天，也许两天？$B肯定没有更久。$B联盟的懦夫从两岛中较大的那座后面冲出来袭击我们。$B他们人太多了，不过我们或许击沉了其中一艘。\n\n我看见另一艘船径直穿过战团，被撕成碎片。$B我猜是地精。$B一群蠢货！' WHERE `ID` = 3574 AND `Text` = 'Day ？？：\r\n\r\nI washed up on the rocky shore of an island.$BIt must be one of the two that I saw before.$BMost of my brothers are dead.$BThere is no sign of our special cargo.$BI fear the worst and cannot believe my thoughts.\r\n\r\nI do not know how many days have passed.$BOne， possibly two？$BSurely not more.$BThe Alliance cowards came at us， hiding from behind the larger of the two islands.$BThere were too many of them， though we might have sunk one.\r\n\r\nI saw another ship sail right through the battle and get torn apart.$BGoblins， I think.$BFools！';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '第？？零一天：\n\n我们在岛上搭起了临时营地。$B阿格拉让我去西岸寻找其他幸存者。$B基拉格将带一小队人翻过山顶搜寻联盟。$B已经有几个人遭到袭击。$B他们不把我们全部杀光就不会停手。$B或者我们把他们都杀光。\n\n远处传来地精的声响，我能看见他们船只的残骸。$B他们真吵。$B我稍后去盯着他们。$B不过先等等——我发现了一个洞穴，里面有奇怪的声响，像是野兽，又像是挖掘。\n\n我要去探个究竟。' WHERE `ID` = 3575 AND `Text` = 'Day ？？and one：\r\n\r\nWe have a makeshift camp atop the island.$BAggra has asked me to look for other survivors on the western shore.$BKilag is to take a small group across the top looking for Alliance.$BAlready a few have attacked us.$BThey will not stop coming until they are all dead.$BOr we are.\r\n\r\nThere are sounds of goblins off in the distance， and I can see the wreckage of their ship.$BThey are noisy.$BI will watch them later.$BFirst， I have found a cavern and strange sounds like animals and mining coming from within it.\r\n\r\nI will investigate.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '收件人：加吉特斯普林太太$B$B随信附上您索要的工业级泻药。对于布利莫·加吉特斯普林先生遭遇悬崖巨人之后的情况，我深表遗憾。我很好奇，您为何选择用泻药而不是某种催吐剂来把他弄回来？在我看来，这对他实在有些不太厚道。祝您如愿以偿！$B$B——洛马克·齿轮条' WHERE `ID` = 3576 AND `Text` = 'Attn：Mrs. Gadgetspring$B$BThe industrial——strength laxative agent you requested is enclosed. My condolences on the fate of Mr. Blimo Gadgetspring after his encounter with the cliff giant. I\'m curious why you\'re opting for a laxative in an effort to recover him， as opposed to some sort of vomit——inducing agent？It seems to me you\'re doing Mr. Gadgetspring a disservice. Good luck with your endeavor！$B$B——Lomac Gearstrip';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '欢迎来到秘密实验室，艾萨拉最引人入胜的新兴旅游胜地！<br /><br /><br />你可曾想过，秘密是从哪里来的？<br /><br /><br />在风景秀丽的艾萨拉富饶森林深处，地精科学家们正辛勤工作，为你发明属于明天的秘密，让你今天就能享用！只需支付少量预付费用，你和全家就能占据前排座位，亲眼观看技艺精湛的地精工程师如何探究并挑逗宇宙的肌理。' WHERE `ID` = 3577 AND `Text` = 'Welcome to the Secret Lab， Azshara\'s most engaging new tourist destination！<br /><br /><br />Have you ever wondered where secrets come from？<br /><br /><br />Deep in the resource——rich forests of scenic Azshara， goblin scientists are hard at work inventing the secrets of tomorrow for you to enjoy today！For just a small up——front fee you and the whole family can get a front——row seat and watch as skilled goblin engineers probe and taunt the very fabric of the cosmos.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '我们为何存在？是什么让我们拥有智慧？在临界失控、释放出足以把行星掀出轨道的冲击波之前，我们能把多少千弗拉普的易爆能量压缩进一立方盎司的危险火箭燃料里？我们可以一起找出答案。你的秘密实验室正等着你！<br /><br /><br /><这份宣传册余下的三十六页，全是繁复的法律免责声明和一份礼品店订购单。>' WHERE `ID` = 3578 AND `Text` = 'Why are we here？What makes us intelligent？How many kilo——fraps of volatile energy can we compress into a cubic ounce of dangerously explosive rocket fuel before it goes critical and unleashes a shockwave capable of tipping the planet off its axis？We can find out together. Your secret lab awaits！<br /><br /><br /><The remaining 36——pages of the brochure consist of complicated legal waivers and a gift shop ordering form.>';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '我们这些头脑敏捷、身体却未必敏捷的人，必须找到……保全自我的替代办法。$B许多这样的人选择投身魔法事业。$B$B$N，我一直在观察你，你的头脑就像钢制的捕兽夹一样敏锐。$B然而，要在这动荡的时代立足，像你这样的人必须掌握奥术技艺。$B而要精通奥术，你就得来跟我谈谈。$B$B来安威玛尔找我吧。$B我们有许多事情要谈。$B$B——提格利·梅罗维斯' WHERE `ID` = 3579 AND `Text` = 'Those of us who are agile of mind， but not quite so agile of body， must find…… alternative methods of self——preservation.$BMany such people choose to pursue a career in matters magical.$B$B$N， I\'ve been observing you， and you have a mind like a steel trap.$BHowever， to thrive in this time of upheaval， a person such as yourself will need to master the arcane arts.$BAnd to master the arcane arts， you\'re going to have to talk to me.$B$BCome speak with me in Anvilmar.$BWe\'ve much to discuss.$B$B——Teegli Merrowith';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '记住这一点：萨满永远不能强求力量——那样会激怒元素，而失去元素庇护的萨满什么都不是。$B行走萨满之路的人绝不能忘记这条最重要的准则。$B$B然而，与元素以互相尊重的方式协作的萨满，所掌握的力量鲜有匹敌者。$B如果你觉得自己怀有这份谦卑，就来安威玛尔找我。$B我会教你——正如我当初被教导的那样——如何与火、土、风、水与荒野之元素共事。$B$B～泰奥·锤暴' WHERE `ID` = 3580 AND `Text` = 'Know this：a shaman must never demand power to do so would arouse the anger of the elements， and a shaman without the elements\' protection is nothing.$BThose that follow the path of the shaman must never forget this most vital tenet.$B$BHowever， a shaman that works in a respectful union with the elements wields a power rivaled by few.$BIf you feel you have the humility to do so， come visit with me in Anvilmar.$BI will teach you——much like I myself was taught——how to work with the elements of fire， earth， wind， water， and the wild.$B$B~Teo Hammerstorm';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '“角色扮演”\n\n出色的角色扮演技巧至关重要。没有哪个聪明的地精姑娘会喜欢一个超级无聊的家伙。用你未来横跨大陆的冒险故事去取悦她：\n\n$B“你和我，宝贝，我们要一起飞往卡利姆多，把我们的名字刻在泰达希尔的侧面，然后在安戈洛环形山的树上度过余生。”\n\n“讲故事”\n\n分享你们未来在一起的精彩故事！越不靠谱越好。没有什么比一个雄心勃勃的计划更能让地精姑娘兴奋了。它也是绝佳的开场话题！\n\n$B“凭我们俩的聪明才智，我们完全可以夺回诺莫瑞根。……话说我们到底为什么还没夺回诺莫瑞根？”' WHERE `ID` = 3581 AND `Text` = '"Roleplaying"\n\nGood roleplaying skills are essential. No Genius Gnomish gal wants a giant bore. Regale her with tales of your future cross——continental adventures：\n\n$B"You and me， babe， we\'re gonna fly to Kalimdor， etch our names into the side of Teldrassil and spend the rest of our lives swinging from the trees in Un\'goro Crater."\n\n"Storytelling"\n\nShare stores of your exciting future together！The more implausible， the better. Nothing gets a Gnomish girl excited like an ambitious plan. It also makes for great conversation starters！\n\n$B"With our brilliant minds combined， we could retake Gnomeregan. …… why haven\'t we retaken Gnomeregan anyways？"';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '“调侃”\n\n调侃是一门用幽默方式取笑女性的艺术。当心，你很容易做得过火。叫她“地精偷袭小飞虫”会让你带着刚买的绿色戈多克格罗格酒独自走回家。试试更含蓄一点的方式。\n\n如果她表现得孩子气，在酒吧中间跳上桌子停不下来，可以试试：\n\n“我听说暴风城孤儿院正在招明星艺员。”\n\n如果她没完没了地谈论自己，可以半开玩笑地试试：\n\n“你的关闭开关在哪儿？”\n\n重要提示：地精姑娘没有关闭开关。试图寻找它可能会让你失去生命、肢体或钱包。' WHERE `ID` = 3582 AND `Text` = '"Teasing"\n\nTeasing is the art of making fun of a woman in a humorous way. Be careful， you can easily go too far. Calling her a "Goblin Ganking Gnat">will leave you walking home wearing that Green Gordok Grog you just bought. Try something a bit more subtle. \n\nIf she acts childish and refuses to stop jumping onto tables in the middle of the bar try：\n\n"I hear there\'s an opening for star entertainer at the Stormwind orphanage."\n\nIf she won\'t stop talking about herself playfully try：\n\n"Where\'s your off switch？"\n\nIMPORTANT NOTE：Gnomish girls do NOT have an off switch. Attempting to find it may result in the loss of life， limbs or wallet.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '你的口味更异域一些？\n你渴望一位来自这世界之外的人吗？\n蹄子正合你意，但魅魔又有点太过了？\n\n继续往下读吧，我的朋友……' WHERE `ID` = 3583 AND `Text` = 'Are your tastes more exotic？\nDo you desire someone a little out of this world？\nAre hooves your thing， but succubi a little too much for you？\n\nRead on， my friend……';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '我刚下船来到秘蓝岛，就在码头附近拦住了一群年约 230 岁、正值妙龄的德莱尼女士。她们正笑着玩得开心。真走运，人还在码头上，我就遇到了此行想结识的那种活泼有活力的德莱尼女性。\n\n起初我有点紧张，我深吸一口气提醒自己：“她们也是来艾泽拉斯度假的，想结识新朋友、玩得开心。”\n\n果然，她们在埃索达见到我这样一个魅力十足的地精很是高兴。后来还发现我们都住在圣光穹顶附近。我们深深地对视，约定当晚晚些时候在阿达尔附近再见面。' WHERE `ID` = 3584 AND `Text` = 'I\'d just arrived off the boat to Azuremyst when I stopped a group of Draenei dames around the ripe young age of 230. They were laughing and having a great time. What luck， still on the docks and I\'d found exactly the type of fun， energetic Draenei women I wanted to meet on this trip. \n\nAt first a bit anxious， I breathed deeply and reminded myself， "they too are here in Azeroth on vacation， looking to meet new people and have a great time."\n\nSure enough， they were delighted to see one devilishly charming Gnome like myself in the Exodar. It even turned out we were both staying near the Vault of Lights. We exchanged deep， penetrating glances into each others eyes， promising to meet again near A\'dal later that night. ';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '第二天，我遇到了另一位美丽的德莱尼女子——她犄角上的光泽只隐约透露出一丝精致的品味。我问她为何来访埃索达，她惊讶地说她不是来访——她就住在这里。\n\n我先前对自己说的话又回到脑中：\n\n“她在度假，想结识出色的人、玩得开心。”$B\n我完全搞错了，她根本不是在度假！然后，我脑中生锈的齿轮突然转动：$B我一直对自己说她们如此热情是因为在度假。多么豺狼人式的借口！\n\n我是个有趣、有意思的人，任何头脑正常的姑娘都会愿意和我组队，不管是不是在度假！现在当我遇到德莱尼姑娘时，我会提醒自己这个简单的道理：\n\n“她也是想结识他人、玩得开心。”' WHERE `ID` = 3585 AND `Text` = 'The next day， I met another beautiful Draenei woman——the gleam of her horns gave only the gentlest of glimpses into her refined tastes. I asked why she was visiting the Exodar， when in shock， she told me she wasn\'t visiting——she lived here. \n\nThe words I spoke to myself before returned to my mind：\n\n"She is on vacation， looking to meet amazing people and have a great time."$B\nI had it all wrong， she wasn\'t on vacation at all！Then suddenly， the grinding gears of my mind clicked：$BI\'d been claiming to myself that they were so receptive because they were on vacation. What a gnollish excuse！\n\nI\'m a fun， interesting guy who any sensible minded girl would love to group with， on vacation or not！Now when I meet Draenei girls， I remind myself of the simple truth：\n\n"She too is looking to meet people and have a great time."';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '这本地图册余下的 497 页，全部是用超级索饵相机 2000 拍下的角度古怪的照片。' WHERE `ID` = 3586 AND `Text` = 'The following 497 pages of this dictionary consistent entirely of oddly angled pictures taken from a Super Snapper FX 2000. ';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '如何与矮人女性约会：\n\n1. 让她请你喝一杯。' WHERE `ID` = 3587 AND `Text` = 'How to date a Dwarven woman：\n\n1. Ask her to buy you a drink.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '说实话，自第三次战争结束以来，暗夜精灵姑娘什么都听过了。$B事实上，在你我出生之前很久，她们就已经什么都听过了。\n\n若想触动一位暗夜精灵姑娘的心智，你必须与众不同。当然，我们都听过暗夜精灵姑娘在邮箱上跳舞、脱衣来支付夜刃豹训练费用的传说。无论真假，若想让那位可爱的女士展露笑容，你必须独特、令人难忘并且自信。\n\n开头要表明你寻找的不只是一个漂亮姑娘。当然，她会蹦会跳，但能不能进行一场像样的谈话？$B她是否懂得萨莫弗莱奇装置的正确用法？她知道怎么玩得开心吗？\n\n没有什么比带着一位暗夜精灵去参加聚会，却只能看着她尴尬地独自站着、偶尔开口只是为了哀叹在上古之战中失去的高等精灵姐妹更糟糕的了。' WHERE `ID` = 3588 AND `Text` = 'Let\'s be honest. Since the end of the Third War， Night Elf girls have heard it all.$BIn fact， they\'d already heard it all long before you or I was born. \n\nIf you want to engage the mind of a Night Elf girl， you\'re going to have to stand out. Sure， we\'ve all heard the tales of Night Elf lasses dancing on mailboxes and stripping to pay for Nightsaber training. True or not， if you want to light that lovely lady\'s lips up with a smile， you gotta be unique， memorable and confident. \n\nStart off by showing that you\'re looking for more than a gal with looks. Sure， she can bounce， she can dance， but can she hold a decent conversation？$BDoes she even understand the proper use of a samophlange？Does she know how to have a fun time？\n\nThere\'s nothing worse than bringing a Night Elf to a party， only to watch her stand awkwardly by herself， breaking conversation only to lament the loss of her Highborne sister during the War of the Ancients.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '没有什么比赢得一位人类姑娘的心更美妙了。人类姑娘无限宽容、无微不至、妙趣横生，古往今来曾是无数英雄的败因。（见第三章：“吉安娜·普罗德摩尔与爱过她的男人们”）\n\n然而，一代又一代人已经证明，想吸引你梦中的女人，光有钱、长相或一身史诗盔甲是不够的。即便是地精发明的力量在这里也帮不上忙。\n\n要真正赢得他人的心，你应当具备这些品质。\n\n* 风趣友善\n* 保持挑战性\n* 像个男人\n\n' WHERE `ID` = 3589 AND `Text` = 'There\'s nothing like wooing the heart of a human girl. Infinitely forgiving， endlessly caring and fantastically fun， human girls have been the downfall of countless heroes throughout the ages.（See Chapter 3："Jaina Proudmoore and the men who loved her"）\n\nHowever， generation after generation has proven it takes something more than just money， looks or an epic suit of armor to attract the woman of your dreams. Not even the power of Gnomish invention can help you here. \n\nTo truly charm the heart of another， you should possess these qualities.\n\n* Be Fun & Friendly\n* Be a Challenge\n* Be a Man\n\n';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '风趣友善\n\n有没有那样的朋友：来你家做客，却把所有人都弄得兴致全无？有，每个人都有。他还会被再次邀请参加聚会吗？除非他带着酒来。如果你想成为有吸引力的人，就过有吸引力的生活。\n\n你会发现，你越享受与人交往，别人也越享受与你交往！\n\n没有什么比带着一副可怜兮兮、满是歉意的气质更快毁掉一个姑娘的夜晚了。放下它，拥抱乐趣，你的自信会随之高涨。' WHERE `ID` = 3590 AND `Text` = 'Be Fun & Friendly\n\nEver have at friend who shows up at your house and brings everybody down？Yep. Everyone does. Does he get invited back to the parties？Not unless he\'s bringing the ale. If you want to be an attractive person， live an attractive lifestyle. \n\nYou\'ll find that the more you enjoy socializing with others， the more they will enjoy socializing with you！\n\nThere\'s no faster way to ruin a girl\'s night than bringing in that needy， apologetic vibe. Let it go， embrace the fun and your confidence will soar.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '保持挑战性\n\n如今有太多地精低垂着头，愁眉苦脸地从一家酒馆挪到另一家，死守着“没有人类姑娘会想要我”这类限制性信念。他们冲进酒馆，对她百般恭维、请她喝酒，然后垂头丧气地回家。\n\n朋友，让我第一个告诉你：当你如此廉价地把自己拱手相送时，你就贬低了自己独特而出众的价值。这个社会告诉你，你不是奖品，女人永远不会认可你，你必须乞求爱与关注。\n\n他们错了。不要那么轻易地付出你的感情。不要问自己“她喜欢我吗？”，而要问自己“我喜欢她吗？”\n\n挑战她——让她看到你寻找的是不止一张漂亮脸蛋的姑娘。如果她跟不上你的生活节奏，就继续前行。如果她展现出值得付出的东西，你就站在一段美好关系的起点上。' WHERE `ID` = 3591 AND `Text` = 'Be a Challenge\n\nToo many Gnomes these days walk with their head slung low， shuffling along sadly from tavern to tavern， hopelessly holding on these limiting beliefs that no human girl would ever want them. They rush into the tavern， shower her with compliments and free drinks， then go home dejected. \n\nWell， let me be the first to tell you， friend， when you give your self away so cheaply， you diminsh the value of your unique， exquisite personality. You\'ve been told by society that you are not the prize， that women will never acknowledge you， that you must beg for love and attention.\n\nThey are wrong. Don\'t give your affection away so freely. Instead of asking yourself， "Does she like me？">ask yourself instead， "Do I like her？">\n\nChallenge her——show her you\'re looking for a girl who offers more than a pretty face. If she can\'t keep up with your life， move on. If she shows she\'s got something to offer， you\'re at the beginning of a beautiful thing. ';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '像个男人\n\n在这个我们被逐出家园、为生存而战、面对艾泽拉斯前所未见的恐怖的时代，你或许以为人们会更懂得男子气概的本质。\n\n遗憾的是，男子气概的艺术已经失落，在战斗的浮华与光鲜中被冲刷殆尽。然而一切尚未失去！通过练习与自信，你可以重新与自己建立连结。\n\n一旦你遇见了梦寐以求的人类姑娘，而她也证明配得上你的情意：\n\n* 主动引导——向她展现你的世界中所有美好之处\n* 牵住她的手——培养亲密而深情的关系\n* 展现尊重——尊重自己、尊重她、尊重你周围的世界\n\n最重要的是：\n\n* 承担责任' WHERE `ID` = 3592 AND `Text` = 'Be a Man\n\nIn an age where we\'ve been banished from our homes， forced to fight for our very survival and faced down horrors never before known to Azeroth， you would think that the nature of manhood would be better understood. \n\nSadly， the art of masculinity has been lost， washed away in the glitz and glamor of battle. However， all is not lost！With practice and confidence， you can come back in touch with yourself. \n\nOnce you\'ve met the human girl of your dreams and she\'s shown herself to be worthy of your affections：\n\n* Take the lead——show her everything that is beautiful about your world\n* Hold her hand——develop a close， affectionate relationship\n* Show respect——for yourself， for her and for the world around you\n\nAbove all：\n\n* Be responsible\n';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '疑难排查\n\n事情并不总按你的预期发展，这正是生活的不可预测与刺激之处。不过有一些技巧能在改善生活方面帮你走很远。以下是一些常见的失误：\n\n* 不要追逐\n* 不要患得患失\n* 不要执着于不喜欢你的人\n\n这些都源自一个核心信念：你必须得到此刻正在交谈的这个女人。挣脱它——这个美丽世界上有那么多女人，如果一个人不合适，就放下。你会发现，你越不黏人，就越有吸引力。' WHERE `ID` = 3593 AND `Text` = 'Troubleshooting\n\nWhile everything doesn\'t always go the way you expect， that\'s what make life unpredictable and exciting. However， there\'s a few tips to help you a long way in improving your life. Here\'s some common blunders：\n\n* Don\'t chase\n* Don\'t be needy\n* Don\'t get stuck on someone who dislikes you\n\nThese all stem from a core belief that women you must have the woman you\'re talking to right now. Break free——there\'s many women out there in this beautiful world and if one doesn\'t work out， let go. You\'ll find you become more attractive the less clingy you are. \n';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '<克劳戈尔的字迹又大又不整齐，比孩童的涂鸦好不了多少。>$B$B那西利——斯西拉——<几处拼写错误被划掉> 异种虫是虫类动物，不是蔬菜（至少在不打架的时候不是）。它们住在地下，除非它们不住在地下。有些还会飞？（我想是的）。$B$B它们的味道非常糟糕。$B$B大多数异种虫由虫子的部件组成。它们的腿在零到八条之间（取决于它们是怎么死的？）' WHERE `ID` = 3594 AND `Text` = '<Crawgol\'s handwriting is large and uneven， little better than a childlike scrawl.>$B$BThe sillu——scilla——<Several misspellings are crossed out> silithid are bug——type animals， not vegetables（at least without a fight）. They live in the under the ground， except when they are not. Some of them fly？（I think）.$B$BThey taste REAL BAD.$B$BMost silithid are made of bug parts. They have between none and eightish legs（depending on how they died？）';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '燃烧能让它们死掉。它们有壳（叫做“&#65533;甲壳&#65533;碎片”，显然是因为由甲壳做成），除非你捅得够用力，否则捅不穿。$B$B它们挖得很快，但我不知道有多快，因为它们在土里挖。$B$B异种虫的起源$B$B几乎所有的异种虫都来自洞穴，通常是地下的洞穴。' WHERE `ID` = 3595 AND `Text` = 'Burning makes them die. They have shells（called &#65533cara pieces&#65533 because they are made from cara obviously）that can\'t be stabbed unless you do it hard.$B$BThey can dig fast but I don\'t know how fast because they dig in the dirt.$B$BTHE ORIGIN OF THE SILITHID$B$BAlmost all silithid come from holes， usually in the ground.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '陶里桑皇帝，\n$B$B以下是我在安戈洛环形山最近的发现记录。$B在大灾变降临后，我中止了当时的项目，开始在整个环形山搜寻新的潜在挖掘点。$B奇怪的是，环形山并未受到大灾变的严重冲击，但我在恐怖之径发现了看似巨型下颚的东西从地面探出！' WHERE `ID` = 3599 AND `Text` = 'Emperor Thaurissan，\n$B$BBelow is my account of my most recent finding here in Un\'Goro Crater.$BAfter the Cataclysm hit， I stopped my current project and began sweeping the Crater for new potential dig sites.$BCuriously， the Crater wasn\'t hard hit by the Cataclysm， but I did find what appeared to be a monstrous mandible peeking out of the ground in Terror Run！';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '它似乎是此地恐龙的一个祖先。$B过去几周我一直在把它挖出来，这是我最激动人心的一次挖掘。$B据我计算，这头巨兽从头到尾将近 300 英尺长。$B这比一些最大的巨龙还要长，也远比环形山现存任何恐龙都大得多。' WHERE `ID` = 3600 AND `Text` = 'It appears to be an ancestor of the dinosaurs that live here.$BI\'ve spent the last several weeks digging it out， and it has been my most exciting dig yet.$BBy my calculations， this beast must be nearly 300 feet long， from tip to tail.$BThat\'s longer than some of the largest dragons， and FAR larger than any dino that currently exists here in the Crater.';
UPDATE `page_text` SET `Text` = '进展缓慢，主要因为我要把身后的工作痕迹掩盖起来。$B那个该死的地精尼尔迈纳还派着手下在附近挖掘，在我把最终结果送回黑石山之前，绝不能泄露这次发现的任何消息。$B这也许就是告诉我们泰坦在安戈洛做了什么的关键信息！$B$B此致敬意，$B$B杜林·暗铲' WHERE `ID` = 3601 AND `Text` = 'The going has been slow， mainly because I\'ve needed to cover up my work behind me.$BThat blasted goblin， Nilminer， still has cronies digging in the area， and I mustn\'t risk any news of this discovery leaking before I send my final results back to Blackrock Mountain.$BThis may be the key piece of information that tells us what the Titans were doing in Un\'Goro！$B$BRegards，$B$BDurrin Direshovel';
